# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor configurations
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Cache and local databases
.claude/
.gemini/
# Everything an agent keeps for itself stays local — except the skills, which are the point of the
# directory: a skill every agent must read before doing the work it covers cannot live where only
# one agent can see it. `.claude/` held the exploratory-test skill until 2026-09-30, so Codex and
# Gemini could not read it, and a Codex session left a headless browser running for three and a half
# hours because the watchdog that skill already had was invisible to it.
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
# The skill's own runtime state: a throwaway browser profile, wiped at every start.
.agents/skills/*/.session/
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Python Environments. `.venv` without a slash: in a gate snapshot (build/snapshot.py) it is a
# symlink to the shared one, and a pattern ending in "/" matches only a directory.
.venv
env/

# Build Outputs
dist/

# Captured test-runner output from the build gate (build/testreport.py)
.build-reports/

# Private working notes that must not ship in a public repo — go-to-market and
# outreach material naming specific gyms, contacts, and competitive tactics.
# The part of that analysis that IS public is in TODO.md.
.private/
